Design Snake Game

(Design + Queue + HashSet + Simulation)

🟢 Problem Statement

Design a Snake Game that supports:

SnakeGame(int width, int height, int[][] food)
int move(String direction)

Rules:

Snake starts at position (0,0)

Initially length = 1

Food is given in order

If snake eats food → grows

If snake hits:

wall ❌

itself ❌

Return -1 (Game Over)

Otherwise return current score (length - 1)

🟢 Example
Input:
width = 3
height = 2
food = [[1,2],[0,1]]

move("R") → 0
move("D") → 0
move("R") → 1
move("U") → 1
move("L") → 2
move("U") → -1

🟢 Key Idea

We need:

1️⃣ Queue → Represents snake body

(head at front)

2️⃣ HashSet → Fast self collision checking
3️⃣ Food Index → Track next food
🟢 Data Structures Used
Structure	Purpose
Deque	Store snake body
HashSet	O(1) collision check
int[][]	Food positions
🟢 Algorithm

For every move:

Get current head

Calculate new head

Check boundary collision

Remove tail temporarily

Check self collision

If food → grow (add tail back)

Add new head

Return score

🟢 Java Code (Interview Level)
import java.util.*;

class SnakeGame {

    int width, height;
    int[][] food;
    int foodIndex;

    Deque<int[]> snake;
    Set<String> set;

    public SnakeGame(int width, int height, int[][] food) {
        this.width = width;
        this.height = height;
        this.food = food;
        this.foodIndex = 0;

        snake = new LinkedList<>();
        snake.add(new int[]{0,0});

        set = new HashSet<>();
        set.add("0,0");
    }

    public int move(String direction) {

        int[] head = snake.peekFirst();
        int x = head[0];
        int y = head[1];

        // Determine new position
        if(direction.equals("U")) x--;
        if(direction.equals("D")) x++;
        if(direction.equals("L")) y--;
        if(direction.equals("R")) y++;

        // Check wall collision
        if(x < 0 || x >= height || y < 0 || y >= width)
            return -1;

        // Remove tail (temporarily)
        int[] tail = snake.peekLast();
        set.remove(tail[0] + "," + tail[1]);

        // Check self collision
        if(set.contains(x + "," + y))
            return -1;

        // Check food
        if(foodIndex < food.length &&
           x == food[foodIndex][0] &&
           y == food[foodIndex][1]) {

            snake.addLast(tail); // add tail back
            set.add(tail[0] + "," + tail[1]);
            foodIndex++;
        }

        // Add new head
        snake.addFirst(new int[]{x,y});
        set.add(x + "," + y);

        return snake.size() - 1;
    }
}

